/**
 * `release_harn.harn` command-line help.
 *
 * Split out of `lib/release_runtime.harn` so the CLI help text, which is pure
 * presentation and grows with every new flag, does not push the runtime module
 * against the 1,500-line handwritten-source ceiling.
 */
pub fn usage() -> string {
  return """
Usage:
  scripts/run_harn_release.sh
  scripts/run_harn_release.sh --agent
  scripts/run_harn_release.sh --mock --agent --mode ship-pr
  scripts/run_harn_release.sh --repo ~/projects/harn --mode prepare --yes-live-release

Modes:
  audit    Inspect release readiness and write an audit report. Default.
  prepare  Run ./scripts/release_ship.sh --prepare --bump <type>.
  ship-pr  Prepare, commit, publish one immutable OID-qualified remote ref,
           tag, open Release vX.Y.Z PR, and enable auto-merge. The local
           release/v$next branch is never published; retries only resume an
           exact immutable remote ref and changed content creates a new one.

Flags:
  --repo PATH             Harn source checkout. Live mutations use an isolated sibling worktree.
                          Defaults to ~/projects/harn.
  --base BRANCH           Base branch for the release PR. Defaults to main.
  --bump TYPE              patch, minor, major, premajor, preminor, prepatch,
                           or prerelease. Defaults to patch.
  --preid IDENTIFIER       Required for prerelease bumps (for example rc or beta);
                           invalid with stable bumps.
  --mode audit|prepare|ship-pr
  --at-sha SHA            Pin the release to a concrete commit on `--base` (default:
                          `origin/<base>` HEAD at startup). Locks the isolated release
                          worktree parent so later base commits cannot enter the
                          published artifact.
  --allow-base-drift      Ship the frozen pin even when its ancestry against
                          `origin/<base>` cannot be proved (dangerous override).
  --expect-pr N           Require PR #N to be present in the selected release range.
                          May be repeated or comma-separated. Also
                          HARN_EXT_RELEASE_EXPECT_PRS.
  --reject-pr N           Refuse to release when PR #N is present in the selected
                          range. May be repeated or comma-separated. Also
                          HARN_EXT_RELEASE_REJECT_PRS.
  --local-audit           Run the complete local audit for diagnosis. Live prepare/ship-pr
                          still requires hosted Windows and macOS certification.
                          Also HARN_EXT_RELEASE_LOCAL_AUDIT=1.
  --agent                 Ask the configured planner to review release evidence with read/search/run tools.
                          Live prepare/ship-pr requires --agent unless CHANGELOG.md
                          already starts with the target version.
  --model MODEL           Model id for --agent. Defaults through HARN_RELEASE_*, shared planner env,
                          then lib/llm_defaults' cloud cell (OpenRouter qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b).
  --provider PROVIDER     LLM provider for --agent. Uses the same default cascade.
  --mock                  Use fake command/file tools for a v0.7.52 -> v0.7.53 release rehearsal.
  --rehearsal             Run the safe release-rehearsal matrix. This uses the
                          mock release path, fail-collects every leg, and writes
                          a report under .harn-runs/release-rehearsal/.
  --bootstrap-new-crates  First release that adds a workspace crate depended on by published crates.
  --focus TEXT            Operator context the model must consider while compiling release notes.
  --yes-live-release      Required for live prepare/ship-pr modes.
  --queue-critical-pr N   Explicit release-critical PR to preserve in the merge queue.
                          Repeat the flag for a dependency chain.
  --queue-live-pr N       Additional PR already in a live merge group; preserve it.
  --queue-noncritical-live-pr N
                          Explicitly allow holding an otherwise-live PR.

Release ownership:
  On macOS, an authorized live prepare/ship-pr invocation is dispatched to the
  canonical hosted Linux workflow before local compilation. Seatbelt cannot
  apply the nested sandbox profiles exercised by candidate certification under
  Harn's default-deny outer sandbox. Audit, mock, and rehearsal runs stay local;
  unsupported live flags fail before dispatch instead of being dropped.
  Live prepare/ship-pr runs acquire Harn's process-owned release-owner host lease
  immediately after pin resolution. Discovery-derived version metadata is
  updated atomically without releasing ownership. Harn recovers the lease only
  after proving that its recorded process died; no sidecar or takeover flag is
  needed.
  Every non-mock run also guards the reusable checkout with one typed
  release-workspace lease. Audits take it opportunistically and otherwise use a
  per-run checkout. A live release waits for an earlier audit, then inherits the
  warm checkout; it never silently falls back and recompiles the workspace.

Chat (interactive postmortem / pre-release review):
  Defaults to ON whenever stdin is a controlling terminal (/dev/tty
  reachable) and the HARN_EXT_CHAT env var is not 0. CI never enters chat
  because /dev/tty is unreachable from a piped/non-TTY context.

  --no-chat               Hard kill switch; skip every chat hook even on a TTY.
  --chat-only             Skip the release pipeline entirely; open the chat
                          loop over a prior run. Use --chat-run to pick one;
                          omit it for a carousel of recent runs.
  --chat-run RUN_ID|DIR   Preselect the run to discuss. Accepts a bare uuid
                          (resolved under .harn-runs/release-harn/), an
                          absolute path to a run dir, or a path to a
                          release-audit.json.
  --chat-timeout-s N      Start-typing timeout in seconds before the chat
                          ends automatically. Defaults to 60.

Credentials (--agent and live prepare/ship-pr):
  Harn reads provider API keys from the environment and does not auto-load
  .env. The canonical launcher loads the configured env files before Harn:
    scripts/run_harn_release.sh --mode ship-pr --agent --yes-live-release
  Discovery order (later overrides earlier): $HARN_EXT_BUMP_FLEET_ENV_FILE
  (default ~/projects/burin-code/.env), $HARN_EXT_BUMP_FLEET_ENV_FILES, ./.env,
  ./.env.local.
"""
}
